From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 999: a disabled bSTA is not a bSTA

config_find_bsta_wireless() matches a wireless section on mode="sta" alone and
never looks at `disabled`. config_generate_bsta_agent() then writes a mapagent
bsta section for it -- ifname, device and band, but no priority, unlike the MLD
path which sets priority, enabled, mld_id and is_mld.

The interface never appears, because it is disabled. What remains is a mapagent
section pointing at nothing, and it cannot be removed: delete it and the next
pass over the radios regenerates it from the same wireless section. The missing
priority then aborts an arithmetic test in /lib/wifi/multiap:

  mapagent[...]: sh: out of range

Measured on hardware 2026-07-28. Every node in the lab carried such sections --
`default_sta_radio0 (ifname=wlan0, disabled=1)` on all three, plus
`default_sta_radio1 (wlan1_0, disabled=1)` on the Pro-8X. Deleting the mapagent
section by hand and watching it come back is what identified this path.

Those wireless sections are sediment: sysupgrade runs keep-config, so a node
carries them across generations, and nothing generates them any more -- they
are in no image, in no map_genconfig, and in neither the wifimngr nor the
mapagent binary. Clearing them is worth doing separately, but the agent should
not have believed them in the first place.

Note this fixes the source, not the symptom. Patch 998 gives the shell a
default so the arithmetic stops failing; this stops the phantom section from
being written at all. They are worth having both: 998 covers any other section
that turns up without a priority.

--- a/src/config.c
+++ b/src/config.c
@@ -4000,7 +4000,7 @@
 
 	uci_foreach_element(&pkg->sections, e) {
 		struct uci_section *s = uci_to_section(e);
-		const char *c_device, *mode;
+		const char *c_device, *mode, *disabled;
 
 		if (strncmp(s->type, UCI_WLAN_IFACE, strlen(UCI_WLAN_IFACE)))
 			continue;
@@ -4013,6 +4013,14 @@
 		if (!mode || strcmp(mode, "sta"))
 			continue;
 
+		/* A disabled bSTA is not a bSTA. Without this the caller
+		 * generates a mapagent bsta section for an interface that is
+		 * never brought up, and that section outlives every attempt to
+		 * remove it because it is regenerated on the next pass. */
+		disabled = uci_lookup_option_string(ctx, s, "disabled");
+		if (disabled && (!strcmp(disabled, "1") || !strcmp(disabled, "true")))
+			continue;
+
 		return s;
 	}
 
